<h3>四、What Happens If You Don't Pay</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Preferred supplier status revoked:</b> Moved to "Approved" tier (5% price disadvantage on future POs)</li>
<li><b>Purchase volume reduction:</b> IKEA will source 40% of your components from alternative suppliers</li>
<li><b>Re-audit required:</b> Full audit (2 days on-site) before reinstatement</li>
<li><b>Public reporting:</b> Your probation status will appear in IKEA's annual Sustainability Report (public document)</li>
</ul>

<h3>五、About the Sustainability Premium</h3>
<p>We understand that a "premium payment" to maintain certification may seem unusual — this is a fair question.</p>
<ul>
<li>The Sustainability Premium funds IKEA's global sustainability improvement programs (we invested €220M in supplier sustainability in 2025)</li>
<li>Similar programs exist at Nike (Sustainable Manufacturing Fund), Unilever (Supplier Sustainability Programme), and Walmart (Project Gigaton)</li>
<li>Payment to the Netherlands entity (rather than Sweden) is required under IKEA's new treasury structure for cross-border sustainability payments</li>
<li>Suppliers who pay the premium see an average score improvement of 12 points in the next audit cycle</li>
</ul>

